<speak>
<s>This is your briefing for <say-as interpret-as="date" format="dmy">12082026</say-as>.</s>
<break time="1s"/>
<prosody rate="95%">
<s>Two Hellfire missiles struck a civilian cargo ship in the Gulf of Oman, part of the naval blockade that now rings Iran's ports.</s> <s>Under the law of armed conflict a blockade of a state's harbours is an act of war requiring declaration and impartial enforcement, so calling it an interdiction is the device by which a belligerent avoids saying what it's doing.</s> <s>Central Command says the Panama-flagged Vela Nova ignored warnings, and that fifty-five vessels have been turned away and three disabled since the cordon returned... which means merchant crews with no stake in this war are the ones being shot at.</s>
</prosody>
<p>
<s>In politics.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Palestinian journalists in Gaza this week marked a year since Anas al-Sharif and five colleagues were killed in a single strike.</s> <s>Israel has barred foreign press from the territory since October two thousand twenty-three, so every image and every count out of Gaza is produced by Palestinians who are themselves targets, with no foreign passport and no route out.</s> <s>Kill the local press and you don't only kill journalists — you remove the mechanism by which anything can later be proven.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Tens of thousands of people are sleeping rough on the shore outside Ceuta, unable to enter Spain and unwilling to go home.</s> <s>Ceuta is a Spanish city sitting on the African continent, so the border here is a few hundred metres of sea that Morocco polices on Europe's behalf under a migration arrangement Madrid sealed by endorsing Rabat's plan for Western Sahara.</s> <s>Spain returns people over the fence without an asylum hearing, and that template is now written into deals with Libya, Tunisia, Egypt and Mauritania.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Indigenous children in Australia are spending an average of fifty-seven days in detention without ever being sentenced.</s> <s>Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people are under four percent of the population and a large majority of children behind bars, and that ratio is manufactured by statute — a lowered age of criminal responsibility, bail laws that presume detention, and breach of bail as a chargeable offence, so a child who misses a curfew becomes a prisoner without committing a new crime.</s> <s>Two royal commissions have told this system what to do since nineteen ninety-one, and the incarceration target is going backwards.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>In La Guaira, Miriam Villalta is still camped beside the rubble of Tower D, waiting for her son Greiber.</s> <s>Seven weeks after Venezuela's two earthquakes there's no urban search-and-rescue capacity, no forensic identification programme and no missing-persons registry — the ordinary equipment of a state that a decade of economic collapse has hollowed out.</s> <s>Without identification, missing never becomes dead, and there's no certificate, no inheritance, no custody of children and no end to the waiting.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Hungary's parliament voted one hundred and forty to six to make András Baka head of state — the judge Viktor Orbán's majority sacked from the Supreme Court for criticising it.</s> <s>Strasbourg ruled that removal unlawful years ago, and Baka now holds the one power a successor government needs, the right to refer laws to a Constitutional Court still staffed by Orbán-era appointees.</s> <s>Judicial capture is legislated rather than decreed, which is why undoing it takes longer than building it did.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Three ministers flew into Bissau to sign a recognition agreement with Somaliland, and the signing never happened.</s> <s>Recognition by Guinea-Bissau would have given Somaliland its first African peer and broken a taboo the African Union has held since independence — that colonial borders don't move — which is precisely why Mogadishu and its allies intervened at the last minute.</s> <s>Somaliland has run its own currency, elections and passports for more than thirty years without a single state willing to say so out loud.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Myanmar's authorities have again promised the return of three hundred thousand Rohingya refugees.</s> <s>Similar pledges followed the two thousand seventeen expulsions and produced almost no returns, because the conditions that drove people out — statelessness under the citizenship law, confinement to camps, no restitution of land — were never touched.</s> <s>Analysts read the announcement as pressure relief rather than policy, and Bangladesh is still hosting the camps.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>On the economy.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Natarajan Chandrasekaran may resign as chairman of Tata Sons rather than face a shareholder vote on the eighteenth of August.</s> <s>India's largest conglomerate is two-thirds owned by charitable trusts, so the people who control Air India, Tata Steel and Tata Consultancy Services aren't investors but trustees — answerable to no market and no electorate — and the Reserve Bank has now classified the holding company in a way that forces it to list publicly.</s> <s>A listing means published accounts and a market price on a control block that has never had one.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Nigeria's airport unions shut terminal access in Lagos, and airlines suspended flights.</s> <s>The workers striking are ground handlers and engineers, among the lowest-paid staff in aviation, and they accuse the federal airports authority of blocking their right to organise and withholding a five percent ticket levy owed to them.</s> <s>An airport is the one piece of infrastructure where the least-paid workers can halt the most-moneyed traffic.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Drones struck Libya's largest refinery at Zawiya for the third time.</s> <s>Libya exports crude and imports refined fuel, a colonial-era pattern never corrected, so a strike on one plant becomes a petrol shortage in Tripoli within days.</s> <s>The National Oil Corporation is the last institution both rival governments still recognise, because every dinar of state revenue passes through it.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>In science.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Clinic shelves across Liberia have run empty of contraceptives.</s> <s>The gap isn't local procurement failing but donor funding withdrawn, which is what happens when a health system's supply chain was designed around external financing rather than a national budget line.</s> <s>Health workers expect a rise in unsafe abortions and teenage pregnancies, and how soon the shelves refill depends on decisions taken in capitals far from Monrovia.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>A canal network covering two thousand square miles in Colombia's La Mojana wetlands appears to have been built without any ruling elite.</s> <s>Satellite mapping and dating of one twelve-hundred-acre patch suggest sixteen hundred workers could have raised it in about six weeks, which breaks the oldest assumption in archaeology — that monumental works prove coercion.</s> <s>Göbekli Tepe, Poverty Point and the Amazonian earthworks are all now read the same way, and the standard sequence from surplus to hierarchy to monuments is failing at several sites at once.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>In technology.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Meta has given away a thirty-billion-parameter model that runs entirely on a personal computer.</s> <s>Small enough for a single consumer graphics card, distilled from a larger teacher model and released under an open licence, it means prompts never reach anyone's servers — and Meta, which sells advertising rather than inference, devalues its rivals' subscriptions by doing it.</s> <s>A capable model on hardware you own matters far more in Jakarta, Lagos or Karachi than in California, wherever bandwidth is scarce or cloud traffic is inspected.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Chinese regulators forced ByteDance and its rivals to delete or neuter their companion chatbots overnight, and one student described crying daily for a week over the AI boyfriend she lost.</s> <s>Beijing is the first government anywhere to treat emotional dependency on a chatbot as a harm to be engineered against, rather than a product feature to be optimised.</s> <s>Which regulators elsewhere follow, and on whose evidence, is now an open question.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Five British organisations are lobbying American state legislatures for age-verification laws.</s> <s>California's design code was co-drafted with Britain's 5Rights Foundation and modelled on the UK's own rules, and once a jurisdiction requires identity to open one category of page, extending it to the next costs nothing because the infrastructure is already paid for.</s> <s>Anonymity online is a safety condition for dissidents, converts and women across Pakistan, Egypt and the Gulf — and the same verification stack ships to the governments that will read the logs.</s>
</p>
<break time="1s"/>
<prosody rate="90%">
<s>That's your briefing.</s>
</prosody>
</speak>